WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.310
<i>As long as good exists in this world,</i>

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.360
<i>so, too, shall evil thrive.</i>

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>Narrator</b>

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>Takashi Hagino</b>

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.690
<i>But behind this eternal 
clash of good and evil,</i>

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.570
<i>there is another battle that goes unseen.</i>

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.210
Blader Crush!

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.000
What?! She blocked the Buster Blade?

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.360
She's growing weapons from her body?!

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.970
What in the world is this monster?!

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.760
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
Assistant: Touka Kuroitsu</b>

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.290
That little one exists to 
read you your last rites!

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.580
The Specialized Counter-Blade Monster!

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.440
Her name is... Mummy!

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.510
<b>Specialized Counter-Blade Monster
Mummy</b>

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.440
We finally did it, Miss Kuroitsu!

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.020
<b>Secret Society Agastia Monster Development Department
New Assistant: Wolf Bete</b>

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.060
Filling a monster with swords 
was a pretty nice idea!

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.510
A blade for a blade.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:50.020
She's the perfect monster to fight Blader.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.580
In that case...

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.240
Second Form!

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.850
Master Blader!

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.670
Master Blade Suigetsu Sen!

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.720
<b>This Week's Weather</b>

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.980
<i>Now for today's special report.</i>

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>A look at the idol duo that 
everyone's talking about: Bavalois.</i>

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.450
<i>We'll be providing an intimate look at the 
pair that just finished a successful concert</i>

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.460
<i>and seems to be everywhere 
on variety shows and dramas.</i>

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.640
There he is, Wolfie boy!

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.830
It's Master Blader!

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.580
<b>UNCERTAINTY WITH THIS YEAR'S FASHION COLORS!? 
MYSTERIOUS FIGURES PLOTTING ALL OVER THE COUNTRY
"WHAT IS JUSTICE, REALLY?" ASKS A NEW ORDER
HOT DOGS ARE DELICIOUS!!
RESTAURANTS WITH THE BEST SUPER-SIZED RAMEN</b>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.120
We finally found you!

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.070
Huh?

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.830
<b>UNCERTAINTY WITH THIS YEAR'S FASHION COLORS!? 
MYSTERIOUS FIGURES PLOTTING ALL OVER THE COUNTRY
"WHAT IS JUSTICE, REALLY?" ASKS A NEW ORDER
HOT DOGS ARE DELICIOUS!!
RESTAURANTS WITH THE BEST SUPER-SIZED RAMEN</b>

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.430
Where'd Mummy go?

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:51.740
Well... actually...

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.990
She just left?!

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.590
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
{}Doctor: Hajime Sadamaki</b>

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.620
Why'd she suddenly run away?

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.630
Was she showing signs of malfunction?

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.620
No, she was making a very good showing.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.560
She's a very powerful monster.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.550
A blade for a blade.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.880
We did design her specifically 
to fight Blader.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.630
Well...

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.510
Personally, I was against the concept of 
designing a monster purely to fight Blader.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.120
It's partly what happened with Banny boy...

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.080
But a monster like that wouldn't have 
much to do after they defeated Blader.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.770
The demands of Mummy's internal mechanisms

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.630
meant we couldn't even give her 
proper vocal capabilities.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.240
I felt a little bad for her.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:41.210
It's true that she's not cut out for many of 
the side tasks Agastia assigns their monsters.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.500
But for now, it's probably best to test out 
a lot of different avenues of development.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.980
There you are, Mummy. Perfect timing.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.440
We were just getting the data together 
in preparation for your next fight—

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:53.270
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:53.360
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:53.440
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:53.520
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.150
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.770
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:55.900
<b>Fighting is boring</b>

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.150
Fighting is boring?

00:02:59.650 --> 00:02:59.740
<b>I wanna be an idol!</b>

00:02:59.740 --> 00:02:59.820
<b>I wanna be an idol!</b>

00:02:59.820 --> 00:02:59.950
<b>I wanna be an idol!</b>

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.410
<b>I wanna be an idol!</b>

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.950
She wants to be an idol?!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.000
<b>— Episode 10 —

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.750
Becoming an idol is no trivial task!

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.820
I-I sorta thought you'd say that.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.660
I'm pleased to see you recognize 
the excellence of Bavalois,

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.050
but their world is unforgiving 
to those who enter it on a whim!

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.770
Yeah, that sounds right.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.860
What even led her to propose such a thing?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.890
<b>Pluripotent Cellular Executive
Immortal Camula</b>

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.040
I wish I knew.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.410
There wasn't anything about 
idols in the virtual memories

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.990
she experienced while we were growing her.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:12.660
I'll lend you a Bavalois concert disc.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.250
But...

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:19.880
No.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.060
That's all I'll say.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.390
Kuroitsu...

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:31.160
This may have revealed a problem with your 
pursuit of flexibility for your monsters.

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.790
I get that you want to let her practice 
dancin' so she can be an idol.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.130
But...

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.750
Why'd you have to ask me for help?!

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:47.460
Well, you seemed like the 
only monster for the job.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.730
With Cannon, it would be...

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.360
With Hydra, it would be...

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.130
With Melty, it would be...

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.930
Please, Wolfie boy!

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:04.410
You're such an incredible athlete!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:04.710
<b>Please</b>

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:04.840
<b>Please</b>

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:04.960
<b>Please</b>

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:05.460
<b>Please</b>

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:07.510
<b>Please</b>

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:07.590
<b>Please</b>

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:09.470
<b>Big Brother Wolf</b>

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:09.590
<b>Big Brother Wolf</b>

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.590
<b>Big Brother Wolf</b>

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:15.710
Well, if you're gonna 
butter me up like that...

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.610
Bring on the dancing!

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.840
C'mon! Let's make you a top idol!

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:59.480
"Hard work can make any dream come true."

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:09.150
<b>Melty girl</b>

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.080
People do find those words attractive,

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:08.460
but can artificial life forms 
be drawn to dreams now, too?

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.120
Do you think Mummy will 
ever be able to sing?

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.640
I doubt it.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.260
She doesn't even have proper vocal cords.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:21.040
It's like asking if you 
could teach a tank to sing.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.800
She just wasn't built for 
anything besides combat.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.460
I'm sure you're right.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.300
But...

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.620
When a human loses a part of their brain,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.520
other parts tend to adapt to compensate.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.170
It's a kind of system redundancy.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.250
It's possible that the same 
might hold true for monsters.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.830
Yeah... maybe.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:58.320
You okay? Are we going too hard?

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.940
Should we ask for a change in choreography?

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.330
<b>Dance!!</b>

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:03.620
C'mon, let's take a break!

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:07.330
Fine, fine. We'll do it.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.840
Where'd this song come from, Wolfie boy?

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:22.600
<b>Dance!!</b>

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.260
We asked a golden boy in the 
industry who works under Agastia

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.170
to work out a song, lyrics, 
and choreography.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:21.410
You're very enterprising, aren't you, Mummy?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:28.190
I think she'll probably get the 
dancing down with enough practice.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.600
But the singing...

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:34.630
But hey, maybe just dancing to the music 
will make a good show on its own.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.110
Okay, Mummy!

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.710
If you're still up for this, 
I'm with you to the end!

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.090
Let's make you an idol!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.230
<i>A monster actively seeking 
a different path...</i>

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:07.810
Monster Data Files

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:07.810
Reiki Sadamaki

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:04.050
<i>I always thought the flexibility 
in their personalities</i>

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:07.050
<i>and abilities came from 
Miss Kuroitsu's designs, but...</i>

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.270
It's a mystery.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.440
I really think you're getting this, Mummy!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:21.830
<b>Sing</b>

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:22.830
<b>Sing</b>

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:26.070
Sing? You wanna practice singing?

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:29.720
But... I'm not sure...

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.170
<b>Sing</b>

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.730
Fine, I get it!

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.780
C'mon, no need to force it.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.810
There's more to being an idol than singing.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.370
Right, Mummy?

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:58.580
Ow!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.480
It's cool, Mummy! I'm fine!

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.440
It's nothin', see?

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.040
Seriously, it's fine...

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.100
Mummy!

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.170
Let me see your wound, Wolfie boy.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.400
Forget me! She's—

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:24.250
Just do it.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.230
<b>Gentle Gauze</b>

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.230
<b>Bandages</b>

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.230
<b>Clear Tape</b>

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:31.310
Why'd you make Mummy to be like that?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.730
There's way too much distance between 
who she is and what she can do.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.170
Even for humans, there's frequently a 
mismatch between what someone wants,

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:41.940
where they end up, and what they can do.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.260
Of course, I didn't think that kind of 
thing would happen with monsters.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:50.610
But she'll be fine if she plays 
to her strengths, like you do.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.050
Hang on a minute!

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:55.260
Did you forget I'm a <i>combat</i> monster?

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:00.040
I feel like I get used for every 
weird, stupid thing <i>but</i> that!

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:19.650
I can't claim to know the strength 
of your determination to be an idol.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:25.780
But seeing a monster made for combat 
aspiring to perform... is absurd.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.960
If you still wish to try, however...

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.140
I shall test your resolve.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:35.320
Allow me to warn you...

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:41.540
I am more than a mere idol fan.

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:43.830
Now, choose!

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.300
Idolhood or death?!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
SPECIALIZED COUNTER-BLADE MONSTER

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
m 56 99 l 259 99 259 116 245 157 185 170 58 170

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
A monster designed to fight Blader. She possesses the ability to
 produce blades from anywhere inside her body, as well as a learning
 function that lets her counter any blade that comes at her. Due to her 
experimental internal mechanism, there was neither space nor
 funding to install voice functionality.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
SPECIAL ABILITIES

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
m 60 203 l 59 225 193 226 224 213 218 202

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
BLADE GENERATION

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
POWER

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
SPEED

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
ENDURANCE

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
COST
PERFORMANCE

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
INTELLIGENCE

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.500
TECHNIQUE

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:48.230
There's a hill I always longed to climb!

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:50.830
Then one day, step by step, I—

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:52.800
That was awesome!

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.760
You've got a pretty nice 
singing voice, Wolfie boy!

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:57.340
That was great!

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.150
Maybe you'd like to be an idol, too?

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:02.610
N-No way! No freakin' way!

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.720
You're not thinking of 
forming a unit with Mummy?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.720
It ain't about that.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:11.860
I was thinkin' you could rig it so 
my voice was comin' out of Mummy.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:15.440
Then it'd sound like she 
was the one singing.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:18.270
I suppose it's possible, but...

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.110
Mummy?

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:25.070
<b>That would be deceiving the audience!</b>

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:24.110
"That would be deceiving the audience."

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:25.260
She's right.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:25.200
<b>That would be deceiving the audience!</b>

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:25.320
<b>That would be deceiving the audience!</b>

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:28.810
People should do things themselves, 
no matter how it turns out.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:25.450
<b>That would be deceiving the audience!</b>

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:33.200
<b>That would be deceiving the audience!</b>

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:33.200
I guess that goes double 
for a human-made monster.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.950
Miss Kuroitsu...

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.450
I had an idea for an idol 
monster a while back.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.830
What happened with you was 
certainly unexpected,

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:45.130
but the Development Department 
would love to gather data

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.370
along your quest to be an idol.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.300
So I'll help you, too.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.470
Let's get you a debut!

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.490
Debut?!

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.860
Every idol needs a debut, right?

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:01.400
Let's hold a small debut event 
and make it a big success!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.840
Yeah!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.410
Mummy!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.640
We've got your event all set up!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:48.150
<b>Monster Idol
Mummy</b>

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:44.040
It's just an event space in one 
of Agastia's affiliate shops,

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.920
but it'll serve just fine for a debut!

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.150
Ain't that great, Mummy?

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:57.410
<b>Monster Idol
Mummy</b>

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:53.160
You've really got the dance moves 
down, so I just know it'll go great!

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.280
Tha...aan...

00:14:57.590 --> 00:15:00.600
Thank... Bibbrother...

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.090
Miz Kurritsu...

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:05.470
Mummy, are you...

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.420
Hang on, is that a voice?!

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:10.950
Miz... Kurritsu...

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.700
Bibbrother!

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.600
Heck yeah! I'm your big brother!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.540
This is awesome!

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:30.030
Where did these changes in 
Mummy's throat come from?

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:34.030
It's too strange to be a 
standard biological reaction.

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:38.180
Is she really forming a voice box?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.120
Do you think...

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.450
What is it, Miss Kuroitsu?

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:47.200
I think I might know what's going on here.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:55.200
Lady Camula, did you implant her 
with your pluripotent cells?

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:01.470
I was opposed to the idea of 
monsters aspiring to perform.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:06.190
Not only would it be stealing 
work that only humans can do,

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:11.870
but a monster designed for that purpose 
would simply become a product showcase.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:16.940
But she was not designed to be an idol.

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:22.780
In a way, she faces a far more 
difficult path than a human would.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:28.040
I simply decided that, if she wishes 
to be an idol despite that difficulty,

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.140
I might as well help her along the way.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:38.940
Nowadays, it's possible to gain a following 
on streaming sites and social media.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:41.780
There's no need to follow the idol's path.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:46.210
If there's one thing that every idol needs,

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:50.860
it's the ability to invigorate those 
around her—a certain sparkle.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:57.210
I believe she may just have that power.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:00.250
Lady Camula...

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.790
But there's a far greater point at issue!

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:07.160
If she does make it as an idol,

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:11.040
it'll mean my cells will be part of an idol!

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:14.870
But it's really not like that! 
That's not why I did it!

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.190
Why did I do something so presumptuous?!

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.560
We've had a lot of trouble getting your cells

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.900
to be compatible with any 
of the monsters we've made.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.940
Why are they working in Mummy?

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:31.410
Logically speaking,

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:33.560
I'd say it's the fact that she's built tough,

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:37.610
and that her body already 
contains multipurpose cells.

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:42.770
But if she really is an idol, is it so 
unbelievable that she'd make a miracle happen?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.880
<b>Monster Idol 
Mummy</b>

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:05.280
Do you think Mummy's voice will be ready?

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.690
She's been getting better 
and better at speaking,

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:11.390
but she's been doing the song 
practice all by herself...

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.240
She really worked hard at the dancing.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:18.550
I think the concert'll be pretty darn good 
with her just dancing to the music, but...

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:47.450
There's a hill I always longed to climb!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:51.640
Then one day, step by step, 
I started getting closer!

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:55.110
But how much work do I need to put in

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:58.520
before my determination finds its reward?

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:03.300
I'm running through the steps 
I just learned! Ready, go!

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:09.190
People can laugh at me and 
say that I'm crazy...

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:14.750
But I just want my voice 
to reach your heart!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.540
Hop, step, miracle! Yeah, yeah!

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.300
Miracles don't happen every day!

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:25.860
But I'll make one for myself! I believe!

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:30.730
With the power you've given me...

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:32.520
I will sing a song!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.650
And I'll do it for you! So watch me, okay?

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:39.540
Smiling for you!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.990
That was awesome!

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:05.450
Hey, everyone!

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:09.020
Thanks so much for being here!

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:12.290
Thank you! Thank you!

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:13.020
Mummy!

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:17.280
There's still a lot we don't know 
about monster development, eh?

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:24.770
Great job!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.770
Welcome back!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.420
Congratulations, Mummy!

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:31.540
Your first concert was a huge success!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:39.300
<b>Thank you both!</b>

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.860
And you didn't even cry 
on stage! Great job, Mummy!

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.940
I know you can only talk a little right now.

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.650
But I know you'll be able 
to talk your head off soon!

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:48.940
And then we'll have an even bigger concert!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:50.430
<b>Thanks, Big Brother!</b>

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.930
<b>Thanks, Big Brother!</b>

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.320
You're soft on your adopted 
little sister, huh?

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.070
Big Brother!

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.470
Hey, shaddap!

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:03.050
I always get treated as a 
little sister or a daughter!

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:05.780
Let me help be supportive of 
someone who's under me for once!

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.200
<b>The golden boy!</b>

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:10.600
The golden boy?

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:14.270
You mean the person who 
wrote the song is here?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.680
It is I!

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.740
Lord Megistus?!

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:23.800
The lyrics, the music, the mixing, 
the choreography, the production...

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.980
It is I who handled them all!

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:31.110
<i>It was a well-known fact in 
certain parts of Agastia</i>

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:33.570
<i>that Megistus was a golden 
boy in the industry.</i>

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.770
<i>She had such a beautiful voice.</i>

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:40.560
<i>But I can't help but feel like 
I've met her somewhere before.</i>

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:45.590
<i>My heart is pounding.</i>

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:48.620
<i>What a strange feeling! 
I've never felt this way before!</i>

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:56.030
<i>He was recalling the terror of fighting her.</i>

